<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Provenance audit &mdash; {{ r.meta.data_checksum }}</title>
<style>
{{ tokens_css }}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--prov-bg);
  color: var(--prov-text);
  font-family: var(--prov-font-ui);
  font-size: var(--prov-size-body);
  line-height: var(--prov-lh-body);
}
.wrap { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--prov-space-7) var(--prov-space-5); }
h1, h2, h3 { font-family: var(--prov-font-display); color: var(--prov-text); margin: 0 0 var(--prov-space-3); }
h1 { font-size: var(--prov-size-display-l); line-height: var(--prov-lh-display-l); }
h2 { font-size: var(--prov-size-heading); line-height: var(--prov-lh-heading); margin-top: var(--prov-space-7); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--prov-border); padding-bottom: var(--prov-space-2); }
h3 { font-size: var(--prov-size-subhead); margin-top: var(--prov-space-5); }
.sub { color: var(--prov-text-tertiary); font-size: var(--prov-size-caption); font-family: var(--prov-font-mono); }
.sub code { color: var(--prov-text-secondary); }
a { color: var(--prov-interactive); }

.strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: var(--prov-space-4); margin: var(--prov-space-5) 0; }
.tile { background: var(--prov-surface); border: 1px solid var(--prov-border); border-radius: var(--prov-radius-lg); padding: var(--prov-space-4); }
.tile .label { font-size: var(--prov-size-caption); color: var(--prov-text-tertiary); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
.tile .value { font-family: var(--prov-font-display); font-size: var(--prov-size-display-l); line-height: 1.1; margin-top: var(--prov-space-2); font-variant-numeric: var(--prov-numeric-table); }
.tile .value.alert { color: var(--prov-state-fault); }
.tile .foot { font-size: var(--prov-size-caption); color: var(--prov-text-tertiary); margin-top: var(--prov-space-1); }

.definition { background: var(--prov-blue-100); border-left: 3px solid var(--prov-interactive); border-radius: var(--prov-radius-md); padding: var(--prov-space-3) var(--prov-space-4); color: var(--prov-text-secondary); font-size: var(--prov-size-body); }

table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: var(--prov-space-3) 0; font-size: var(--prov-size-data); font-variant-numeric: var(--prov-numeric-table); }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: var(--prov-space-2) var(--prov-space-3); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--prov-border); vertical-align: top; }
th { color: var(--prov-text-tertiary); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: var(--prov-size-micro); letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
tbody tr:hover { background: var(--prov-surface-hover); }

.pill { display: inline-block; padding: 1px var(--prov-space-2); border-radius: var(--prov-radius-md); font-size: var(--prov-size-micro); font-family: var(--prov-font-mono); border: 1px solid transparent; }
.sev-critical { background: var(--prov-red-100); color: var(--prov-state-fault); border-color: var(--prov-red-500); }
.sev-high { background: var(--prov-amber-100); color: var(--prov-amber-700); border-color: var(--prov-amber-500); }
.sev-medium { background: var(--prov-slate-100); color: var(--prov-text-secondary); }
.sev-low, .sev-info { background: var(--prov-slate-100); color: var(--prov-text-tertiary); }
.no-count { color: var(--prov-state-verified); font-family: var(--prov-font-mono); font-size: var(--prov-size-micro); }

.evidence { font-family: var(--prov-font-mono); font-size: var(--prov-size-micro); color: var(--prov-text-secondary); white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
details { margin: var(--prov-space-1) 0; }
summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--prov-interactive); font-size: var(--prov-size-caption); }
pre { background: var(--prov-slate-100); border-radius: var(--prov-radius-md); padding: var(--prov-space-4); overflow-x: auto; font-family: var(--prov-font-mono); font-size: var(--prov-size-micro); color: var(--prov-text-secondary); }
footer { margin-top: var(--prov-space-8); color: var(--prov-text-tertiary); font-size: var(--prov-size-caption); border-top: 1px solid var(--prov-border); padding-top: var(--prov-space-3); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <h1>Provenance audit</h1>
  <div class="sub">
    generated {{ r.meta.generated_at }} &middot;
    code <code>{{ r.meta.code_version }}</code> &middot;
    config <code>{{ r.meta.config_hash }}</code> &middot;
    data <code>{{ r.meta.data_checksum }}</code>
  </div>
  <div class="sub">window {{ cov.window_start }} &rarr; {{ cov.window_end }}</div>

  <div class="strip">
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="label">Readings</div>
      <div class="value">{{ "{:,}".format(r.meta.n_rows) }}</div>
      <div class="foot">{{ cov.n_stations }} stations &middot; {{ cov.n_covered_pairs }} covered series</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="label">Conventional completeness</div>
      <div class="value">{{ "%.2f"|format(cov.conventional_completeness_pct) }}%</div>
      <div class="foot">non-null share &mdash; looks healthy</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="label">Defective cells</div>
      <div class="value alert">{{ "{:,}".format(dr.n_defective_cells) }}</div>
      <div class="foot">of {{ "{:,}".format(dr.n_covered_cells) }} covered cells</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="label">Defect rate</div>
      <div class="value alert">{{ "%.2f"|format(dr.percent) }}%</div>
      <div class="foot">grid completeness {{ "%.2f"|format(cov.grid_completeness_pct) }}%</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="definition">{{ dr.definition }}</div>

  <h2>Defects by reason code</h2>
  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Name</th><th>Category</th><th>Severity</th><th>Counts?</th><th class="num">Count</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for code in r.defects_by_code|sort %}
      {% set rc = codes[code] %}
      <tr>
        <td><code>{{ code }}</code></td>
        <td>{{ rc.name }}</td>
        <td>{{ rc.category }}</td>
        <td><span class="pill sev-{{ rc.severity }}">{{ rc.severity }}</span></td>
        <td>{% if rc.counts_toward_defect_rate %}yes{% else %}<span class="no-count">coverage</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(r.defects_by_code[code]) }}</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Coverage</h2>
  <p class="sub">Four quantities kept strictly separate. Structural absences are excluded from the defect rate.</p>
  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Quantity</th><th class="num">Cells</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Observed</td><td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(cov.n_observed_cells) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Absent (R01)</td><td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(cov.n_absent_cells) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Covered = observed + absent</td><td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(cov.n_covered_cells) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Structurally excluded</td><td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(cov.n_structurally_excluded_cells) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Expected = covered + structural</td><td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(cov.n_expected_cells) }}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Structural absences <span class="sub">coverage facts, not defects</span></h2>
  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Station</th><th>Parameter</th><th>Domain</th><th>Code</th><th class="num">Excluded cells</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for s in r.structural_absences %}
      <tr><td>{{ s.station_id }}</td><td>{{ s.parameter }}</td><td>{{ s.domain }}</td><td><code>{{ s.reason_code }}</code></td><td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(s.excluded_cells) }}</td></tr>
    {% else %}
      <tr><td colspan="5">None.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Notable events</h2>
  <p class="sub">Ranked by physical severity, then magnitude. Each carries the evidence that flagged it.</p>
  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th class="num">#</th><th>Code</th><th>Station</th><th>Parameter</th><th>Timestamp (UTC)</th><th>What &amp; evidence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for e in r.notable_events %}
      <tr>
        <td class="num">{{ e.rank }}</td>
        <td><span class="pill sev-{{ e.severity }}">{{ e.reason_code }}</span></td>
        <td>{{ e.station_id }}</td>
        <td>{{ e.parameter }}</td>
        <td>{{ e.timestamp_utc }}</td>
        <td>
          {{ e.headline }}
          <details><summary>evidence</summary><div class="evidence">{% for k, v in e.evidence.items() %}{{ k }}: {{ v }}
{% endfor %}</div></details>
        </td>
      </tr>
    {% else %}
      <tr><td colspan="6">None.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Defects by station</h2>
  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Station</th><th class="num">Defective flags</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for station in r.defects_by_station|sort %}
      <tr><td>{{ station }}</td><td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(r.defects_by_station[station]) }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Appendix: thresholds used</h2>
  <p class="sub">Every value the detectors depended on, with its cited basis. This is the answer to &ldquo;how did you get that number?&rdquo;</p>
  <pre>{{ r.thresholds | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre>

  <footer>
    Provenance &mdash; AI trust layer for environmental data. Statistics-only audit (B1). No machine learning in this report.
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
